-- title:
--   Existence of an irreducible symmetric modular polynomial Φ_ℓ
-- statement:
--   Let $\ell$ be a prime. The assertion is that there exists a term `data` of the structure `ModularPolynomialData ℓ`, that is, a polynomial $\Phi =$ `data.Φ` in $(\mathbb{Z}[X])[Y]$ which is monic, whose degree in $Y$ equals `dedekindPsi ℓ`, the sum of $\ell/d$ over the squarefree divisors $d$ of $\ell$ (so $\ell+1$), and which satisfies $\Phi.\mathrm{eval}_2(\mathrm{evalAtJ}, \mathrm{jqN}\ \ell) = 0$, where `evalAtJ` is the ring homomorphism $\mathbb{Z}[X] \to$ `LaurentSeries ℚ` evaluating a coefficient polynomial at the Laurent series `jq`, and `jqN ℓ` is the Laurent series of that name; and such that this same packet has both of the following two properties. First, `PhiIrreducible data`: the polynomial `data.toAdjoin`, obtained from $\Phi$ by mapping its coefficients through `evalAtJGen` into the intermediate field $\mathbb{Q}\langle\mathrm{jq}\rangle$ generated by `jq`, is irreducible over that field. Second, `EvalSymm data.Φ`: for all Laurent series $x, y$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, evaluating $\Phi$ by substituting $x$ into the coefficient polynomials and $y$ into the outer variable gives the same result as substituting $y$ into the coefficients and $x$ into the outer variable.
--
--   This is the existence, for each prime $\ell$, of the classical modular polynomial $\Phi_\ell(X,Y)$ relating $j(q)$ and $j(q^\ell)$, in the strong form in which irreducibility over $\mathbb{Q}(j)$ and the symmetry $\Phi_\ell(X,Y)=\Phi_\ell(Y,X)$ hold for one and the same packet; the pair of properties is what pins the packet down. It feeds the uniqueness statement [`ModularCurve.ModularPolynomialData.eq_of_prime`](thm.html#ModularCurve.ModularPolynomialData.eq_of_prime), the construction of the Fricke involution [`ModularCurve.exists_isFrickeAut`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_isFrickeAut), and the existence of a monic relation [`ModularCurve.exists_monic_evalAtJ_jqN_eq_zero`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_monic_evalAtJ_jqN_eq_zero).
